From: mscharged-port
Subject: Narrow online scene button contexts natively
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility

The online hub, friends, friend code entry, invitation, Mii selection,
side choice and connection quality scenes store each pointer button's
index in its void* context and read it back with (int)context or
(unsigned int)context. A 64-bit host rejects those casts from a pointer
to a smaller integer. Natively the index goes through std::intptr_t, as
in the Cup scenes (0641); the values are unchanged.

